name pair-formation-1
timeout 900

# THE STATION-KEEPING RIG, and nothing else: no opponent, no weapons, no radar. A two-ship in which
# the LEAD flies a route with two hard turns and the WINGMAN does nothing but hold its combat-spread
# station on him. It is the mission that measures doc/formation.md section 4 in isolation, the way
# mig29-radar-notch measures a Doppler envelope in isolation.
#
# WHAT THE WINGMAN IS ACTUALLY HOLDING is a MESSAGE, not a position: the lead's PPLI, one per second,
# held up to three cycles. At 300 kt that is 460 m of pure report age, which is why the declared spread
# (1 nm) has to be several times it.
#
# THE CONTROL LAW, in two channels that never talk to each other (that separation IS the law):
#   across + vertical  the path following that already exists — FBAutopilot::SetDirectLeg onto the
#                      lead's COURSE LINE THROUGH the station. The wingman therefore regulates a
#                      cross-track distance to a LINE, never a bearing to a point, and cannot enter the
#                      pursuit oscillation a moving aim point produces.
#   along              the throttle, and the commanded closure is the one this airframe can still
#                      cancel over the remaining distance: dv = sqrt(2 * BfmBrakeMs2() * |e_along|),
#                      capped at sqrt(2 * a * spread). No gain, no time constant, no integrator.
#
# READING RULE: exit 0 (SUCCESS) — the LEAD's waypoints are the mission, and the wingman declares
# `objective survive` only, so it is judged on being alive rather than on flying a route of its own
# (it has none: its route is its leader). What is measured is `flt_sta` in telemetry_two.csv, the
# station error in metres, sampled every tick the station is being held and -1 otherwise:
#   the steady-state value on a straight leg  = how well the two channels hold
#   the peak through each 90-degree turn      = what a turning lead costs, and it is a REAL cost,
#                                               because the station swings through the turn radius
#   whether it returns                        = that the law has no standing offset
# `flt_mates` is 1 for the whole run (the lead is heard), `flt_assign` 0 throughout (nothing to sort).
#
# MEASURED: straight-leg station error 45.2 m median / 84.4 m max over the final 3,400 ticks; through
# each 90-degree turn 1,936.7 m and 1,909.6 m peak, both recovered; 63.5 m median over the whole run.
# No standing offset: the third leg settles at 45 m and stays there.

unit lead
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight rig 1
  spawn 46.90000 6.40000 6000 90.0 350
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set datalink on
  wp 46.90000 6.90000 6000 350          # straight east, ~38 km
  wp 47.20000 7.10000 6000 350          # hard left, north-east
  wp 47.20000 7.60000 6000 350          # hard right, east again
  objective waypoints
  objective survive

unit two
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight rig 2
  spawn 46.88334 6.40000 6150 90.0 350  # on station: 1 nm right of the lead's track, 150 m stacked
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set datalink on
  set task formation
  objective survive
